       'A homeowner has a 2% wind deductible on a dwelling insured for $350,000. Hail causes $12,000 of damage. What is paid?', 'A percentage deductible is taken on the **insured value**, not on the loss: 2% × $350,000 = $7,000, so $12,000 − $7,000 = **$5,000**. $11,760 is 2% of the loss deducted instead — the mistake the question is built to catch.', 'draft'
  from public.courses c
