       'Under split limits of 250/500/100, three people are injured with bodily injury claims of $200,000, $200,000 and $150,000. What does the policy pay for bodily injury?', 'Each claim is within the $250,000 per-person limit, so none is individually capped — but they total $550,000 against a $500,000 per-accident limit, so **$500,000** is paid. $550,000 ignores the per-accident limit; $250,000 applies the per-person limit to the total.', 'draft'
